Build "TrainLog": a local-first, mobile-first workout tracker using React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind CSS + Recharts. It must work as an installable PWA and be ready to wrap with Capacitor for Android/iOS later. It tracks gym, calisthenics, martial arts and cardio training, groups exercises into named collections, schedules workouts with reminders, and shows progress, muscle balance and achievements.

WORKING METHOD
Build in phases. Do ONLY Phase 1 now, then stop and wait for me to say "continue".
Phase 1: foundation (architecture, tokens, themes, i18n/RTL, services, domain functions + unit tests, data model, seed data, navigation shell, onboarding, settings)
Phase 2: Library (Exercises | Collections), Add/Edit Exercise, Collection Detail
Phase 3: Active Workout (all tracking types), logging engine, PR detection and celebration, Workout Summary, draft autosave and resume
Phase 4: Home, Calendar and schedules, reminders, streak, XP/level, achievements
Phase 5: Progress (Exercise and Overview modes), muscle hexagon, anatomical heatmap, body measurements
Phase 6: motion polish, PWA, README

