ARCHITECTURE
- Every platform feature sits behind a service interface with a web and a native implementation, chosen at runtime via Capacitor.isNativePlatform():
  a) StorageService: IndexedDB on web, Capacitor Preferences/SQLite natively. Schema is versioned (schemaVersion + migrations), and export files carry the version. ALL weights are stored in kg and converted only for display.
  b) NotificationService: scheduleReminder, cancelReminder, rescheduleAll. @capacitor/local-notifications natively; web Notification API + an in-app "You have a workout today" banner as fallback. Call rescheduleAll whenever a schedule changes and whenever the app opens. Never block the UI on a permission prompt; show a friendly explainer first.
  c) HapticsService (Capacitor Haptics / navigator.vibrate), SoundService (set beep, rest-end beep, round bell, PR sound).
  d) KeepAwakeService (@capacitor-community/keep-awake natively, Screen Wake Lock API on web), active during a workout.
  e) ShareService (Capacitor Share natively, Web Share API with a copy/download fallback).
- Capacitor-ready: relative asset paths, output in /dist, no runtime CDN dependencies, no browser-only API without a fallback.
- Domain layer: all calculations (formulas below) are pure, typed functions in /domain with Vitest unit tests (epley1RM, workingVolume, detectPRs, smartTarget, muscleLoad, regionValues, recovery, streak, xp, estimateMinutes, kcal).
- Timers (elapsed, rest, round) are computed from stored timestamps, never from a ticking counter, so they stay correct when the app is backgrounded.

DATA MODEL
- Exercise {id, name, category, equipment, primaryMuscles[], secondaryMuscles[], conditioning (boolean, for cardio with no muscle target), trackingType, defaultRestSec, defaultRepMin/Max, incrementKg, roundConfig {roundSec, restSec, rounds} (rounds type only), notes, videoUrl, isPinned, isArchived, source: builtin|custom}
- trackingType: weight_reps | bodyweight (signed load: +added or -assisted) | reps | duration | distance_time | rounds
- equipment: barbell|dumbbell|machine|cable|kettlebell|bodyweight|band|bag|cardio_machine|other
- Collection {id, name, goal: strength|hypertrophy|endurance|power|skill|conditioning, items[]}; CollectionItem {exerciseId, role: warmup|compound|isolation|finisher|skill|cooldown, sets, repsMin, repsMax, restSec, note}
- Goal presets (prefill only): Strength 3-6 reps / 150-180s rest, Hypertrophy 6-12 / 60-90s, Endurance 15+ / 30-45s.
- Session {id, number, startedAt, endedAt, pausedMs, collectionId?, locationId?, effort, notes, xpGained, sets[]}; SetEntry {exerciseId, loadKg (signed for bodyweight), reps, durationSec, distanceM, rounds, rpe (0.5 steps), tag: normal|warmup|drop|failure, done}
- Schedule {mode: weekly|cycle, days[] or cycle[], time, reminderOn, collectionId}; BodyMeasurement; Location {id, name} (user-named places only, NO GPS, no city); Achievement; Settings; ActiveSessionDraft.
- 18 muscle groups (one i18n dictionary used on every screen): chest, traps, lats, lower_back, front_delts, side_delts, rear_delts, biceps, triceps, forearms, abs, obliques, glutes, quads, hamstrings, calves, adductors, hip_flexors.
- 6 regions: Chest=[chest]; Delts=[front_delts, side_delts, rear_delts]; Arms=[biceps, triceps]; Back=[lats, traps, lower_back]; Legs=[quads, hamstrings, glutes, calves]; Core=[abs, obliques]. Forearms, adductors, hip_flexors appear only on the heatmap. REGION_ORDER (clockwise from top) is a single constant used everywhere: Chest, Delts, Arms, Back, Legs, Core.

