DEVIATIONS FROM THE REFERENCE (important)
1. FLAT ONLY: no backdrop-blur, no blur filters, no drop shadows. Separation comes from borders and tone steps. The hero-card glow is a CSS radial-gradient (accent at ~12% opacity), not a blurred element.
2. NO EXTERNAL ASSETS: no Tailwind CDN (compile with Vite), no Google Fonts, no Material Symbols font, no hosted photos.
3. RTL: logical utilities only (ms-, me-, ps-, pe-, start-, end-, text-start, border-s). Timers, numbers and chart geometry stay LTR; chevrons, nav and layouts mirror. English and Arabic through a lightweight i18n dictionary; numbers stay Western digits.
4. NO HARDCODED SAMPLE DATA: dates, names, streaks, counts, units, session numbers, places all come from real data (e.g. "35 lbs" follows the unit setting; "240+ exercises" is computed). The name is optional from onboarding; the greeting omits it if empty. Times show mm:ss under one hour and h:mm:ss after.
5. Selected states = accent (or category) border + 10% tint + check icon, never a faint fill change.
6. Names wrap to 2 lines in list rows (no "Barbell Bench ..."); stat tiles wrap or shrink instead of overflowing; chart labels stay inside the viewBox with padding.
7. Rename "AI Target" to "Smart target" (it is a rule, not an AI model). Remove "Top 5% intensity" claims (see PR rules).
8. Future sets in a workout are dimmed but editable, never locked.
9. Heatmap/hexagon color is never the only signal: always show the % or set count.

FORMULAS (use exactly these; show "est." where approximate)
- Est. 1RM (Epley) = weight x (1 + reps/30); reps = 1 -> weight; ignore sets above 12 reps. For bodyweight exercises use bodyweight + signed load when bodyweight is known.
- Volume = sum of weight x reps over done, non-warm-up sets (bodyweight: (bodyweight + load) x reps when known). Warm-up sets are excluded from volume, PRs and muscle load. "Sets done" counts working sets against planned working sets; warm-ups are noted separately.
- PR types (per exercise, working sets only): Weight PR = heaviest weight in a set; Reps PR = most reps in one set at the same or heavier weight than the previous best-reps set (or most reps for reps-only/bodyweight); Est. 1RM PR; Volume PR = best total volume of that exercise in one session. Rounds PR = most rounds at the same round length. Timed PR = longest duration; distance PR = best distance or pace.
- PR celebration timing (Settings: Instantly | After exercise (default) | At finish): a "NEW PR" badge and light haptic appear on the set row immediately in all modes; the full overlay appears at the chosen moment, queued if several. Never interrupt a running rest timer.
- Smart target: if all working sets last time reached the top of the target rep range at RPE <= 8.5, suggest +incrementKg (default 2.5 kg / 5 lb); otherwise suggest +1 rep at the same weight. "Apply target" pre-fills set 1.
- Calories (est.) = MET x bodyweight kg x hours. MET: Gym 5, Calisthenics 6, Martial Arts 8, Cardio 8. Default bodyweight 75 kg if unknown. Settings toggle to hide.
- Estimated collection time (min) = sum over items of sets x (45s + restSec) / 60, rounded to 5.
- Muscle load: a working set counts 1 on each primary muscle and 0.5 on each secondary. Weekly average sets = weighted sets in the window / (days / 7). Muscle % = weekly average / weekly target (Settings, default 14 per muscle) x 100.
- Bands: Deficit < 60%, Maintenance 60-99%, Optimal 100-120%, Peak > 120%.
- Region % = mean of its muscles' % (each capped at 150% for the mean). If a region is >= 100% but one of its muscles is < 60%, show an "uneven" note naming the weakest muscle (e.g. "Triceps low").
- Balance score = muscles at >= 60% / 18 x 100.
- Recovery per muscle = min(100, hoursSinceLastTrained / recoveryHours x 100); recoveryHours = 48, or 72 if that muscle had 8+ working sets or avg RPE >= 9 in its last session. Never trained = 100. Labels: >= 90 Primed, 70-89 Recovered, 50-69 Recovering, < 50 Fatigued. Region recovery = mean of its muscles; Overall readiness = mean of the six regions (>= 80 Optimal, 60-79 Moderate, < 60 Low). Always labeled as an estimate.
- Session region impact (Summary): the session's weighted sets per region as a % of the weekly target for that region.
- Auto-rebalance: for the (up to) 2 lowest regions under 100%, missing sets = (target - weekly avg) per deficit muscle, capped at 6 per region. Show e.g. "+4 sets Pull, +3 sets Posterior". "Apply" opens a preview sheet with suggested exercises (primary muscle = the deficit muscle, prefer ones the user has logged) and set counts; on confirm they are added to the next planned collection. Never change a workout silently.
- XP: 100 per completed workout + 10 per working set + 50 per PR. XP to next level = 300 + 50 x level. Ranks: 1-4 Starter, 5-9 Regular, 10-19 Athlete, 20-29 Elite Lifter, 30+ Legend.
- Streak: a day counts if it has a completed workout, is an unscheduled/marked rest day, or is covered by a freeze. A missed scheduled workout breaks it. One automatic freeze per week. With no schedule, the streak continues while the gap between workouts is <= 2 days.
- Percentile claims ("Top x% of your sessions") appear only once the user has 10+ sessions; otherwise show "Session #N". For PR context use "first <exercise> PR in N days" (days since the previous PR).

MUSCLE HEXAGON (shared <MuscleHexagon> component, plain SVG, no chart library)
- 6 axes in REGION_ORDER, vertex i at angle -90 + 60 x i degrees. Radius = R x min(pct, 150) / 150. Concentric rings at 50%, 100% (dashed accent, labeled "100% target") and 150% (outer edge). Filled polygon (accent ~20% opacity, accent stroke); one dot per vertex in BAND_COLORS; label = region name + %. Keep labels inside the viewBox.
- Props: values[6], mode (volume|recovery), compareValues? (previous period, dashed outline), size (sm|md), showLabels, onSelectRegion. Size sm uses 3-letter labels (CHE, DEL, ARM, BAC, LEG, COR) and status chips beside it. aria-label summarizes all six values and bands. Chart geometry stays LTR in RTL; label text is translated.
- Insight line, computed: "Back and Legs are lagging below target, while Chest is peaking" (regions < 60% and > 120%); if all are 100-120%: "Well balanced".
- Used in: Home (recovery mode, sm), Progress > Overview (md, volume | recovery toggle, "Prev" compare switch), Workout Summary (sm, session impact), Collection Detail ("Muscle coverage", sm, collapsible; uses the collection's target sets per region, no history needed).

